# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What never enters the Docker build context.
#
# The build context is the whole directory tree, sent to the Docker daemon
# BEFORE the first instruction runs. Everything listed here would otherwise
# travel across that boundary even though the Dockerfile only ever copies one
# file (requirements.lock.txt).
#
# The first block is the reason this file exists at all: a build context is
# not a secret-free zone, and .env has no business being in one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large and useless here. The code is bind-mounted at run time, not copied in,
# so none of this would end up in the image anyway -- but it would all be
# uploaded to the daemon on every single build, on a 2-vCPU server.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The APCIQ PDF archive: ~200 MB, and a licence that forbids redistribution.
data/
var/

# dbt artefacts, regenerated on every run.
dbt/target/
dbt/logs/
dbt/dbt_packages/

# Power BI files. The .pbix carries its data compressed inside the file.
*.pbix
**/.pbi/cache.abf
**/.pbi/localSettings.json

# Documentation and design notes: not needed to install dependencies.
docs/
powerbi/
notebooks/
sample_data/
*.md
